      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.36,
      "end_seconds": 10.57,
      "duration_seconds": 9.21,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, doctor, hi, where would you like me to put my coat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.28,
      "end_seconds": 17.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.36,
      "end_seconds": 60.72,
      "duration_seconds": 39.36,
      "text": "Let me think, uh, honestly, it's it stopping just as suddenly, and my family pushed me to come. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. Oh, um, and my heart suddenly racing. Okay, you know, so with my heart suddenly racing, I get some relief from cold water on the face. Well, I've been feeling lightheaded during an episode too, for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.61,
      "end_seconds": 72.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.55,
      "end_seconds": 80.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.5,
      "end_seconds": 103.65,
      "duration_seconds": 13.15,
      "text": "Okay: weight 94 kilos, BMI works out to 34.9, temp 36.7 degrees, pulse is 71 beats a minute, pressure 118 over 78, height 164 centimetres."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.35,
      "end_seconds": 107.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Is that alright, you know, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.74,
      "end_seconds": 111.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Alright, I'll come back to the numbers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.32,
      "end_seconds": 117.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "right, let's have a proper look at you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.84,
      "end_seconds": 120.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "hold that for a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.98,
      "end_seconds": 137.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Your heart sounds and rhythm are normal today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.85,
      "end_seconds": 143.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.16,
      "end_seconds": 164.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "any breathlessness, chest pain, family history of sudden death or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.04,
      "end_seconds": 170.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Uh, none of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.68,
      "end_seconds": 173.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.63,
      "end_seconds": 178.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "No, you know, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.88,
      "end_seconds": 181.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.79,
      "end_seconds": 186.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.72,
      "end_seconds": 195.18,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "Alright, diabetes, that matches what I have here. Any regular medication, tablets or creams?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.43,
      "end_seconds": 204.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "hmm, no, I don't take any tablets"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.83,
      "end_seconds": 208.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.48,
      "end_seconds": 211.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.99,
      "end_seconds": 214.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.45,
      "end_seconds": 219.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.17,
      "end_seconds": 222.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.29,
      "end_seconds": 226.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.76,
      "end_seconds": 229.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Right, have you retired yet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.1,
      "end_seconds": 236.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.48,
      "end_seconds": 263.86,
      "duration_seconds": 9.38,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? The most likely explanation is episodes of supraventricular tachycardia. Atrial fibrillation is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.78,
      "end_seconds": 269.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.66,
      "end_seconds": 290.56,
      "duration_seconds": 19.9,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's episodes of supraventricular tachycardia, and we'll know more once the a 7-day heart monitor is back. Stop me if I've got anything wrong. You've had it stopping just as suddenly, and no breathlessness or chest pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.23,
      "end_seconds": 293.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "yes, you've got it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.52,
      "end_seconds": 327.67,
      "duration_seconds": 32.15,
      "text": "A 7-day heart monitor is what I'd like next, for paroxysmal palpitations. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. An ECG is what I'd like next, for palpitations. Try blowing hard against a closed mouth and nose when it starts. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. Do get help quickly if the symptoms get worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.33,
      "end_seconds": 335.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "I'd like you back after the monitor. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 337.12,
      "end_seconds": 338.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.64,
      "end_seconds": 340.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "all the best"
    }
  ]
